{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/SOAP Web Service.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/SOAP Web Service.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"soap web service soap web service","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/SOAP Web Service.md","fileName":"SOAP Web Service.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"SOAP Web Service","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-22 23:34\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[HTTP FTP SMTP and Custom Protocols]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["HTTP FTP SMTP and Custom Protocols","hands-onsoftwarearchitecturewithc8andnetcore3.pdf","hands-onnetworkprogrammingwithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/SOAP Web Service.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/SOAP Web Service.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"soap web service soap web service","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/SOAP Web Service.md","fileName":"SOAP Web Service.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"SOAP Web Service","heading":"SOAP Web Service","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A SOAP web service exchanges structured messages according to the Simple Object Access Protocol. SOAP defines an application-level messaging contract above the transport and is commonly carried through HTTP rather than replacing HTTP's network role.\n\nThe contract can standardize operations and message structure across consumers, but its additional envelope and service conventions are useful only when both sides need that formal interoperability.\n\nThe architecture source presents SOAP as a standards-based service approach with structured envelopes and formal contracts suited to established enterprise interoperability needs, while contrasting its heavier protocol model with common REST interfaces.","tags":["baby"],"links":["HTTP FTP SMTP and Custom Protocols","hands-onsoftwarearchitecturewithc8andnetco